{"name":"Durango Dust","hex":"#fbe3a1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dust","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Fine particles.\n Fine, dry particles of matter found in the air and covering the surface of objects, typically consisting of soil lifted up by the wind, pollen, hair, fiber debris, dead skin cells, etc.\n\n Any substance reduced to fine particles; powder.\n Submicron particles in outer space, largely silicates and carbon compounds, that contribute greatly to extinction at visible wavelengths.\n\n Disintegration of a solid, like silica.\n Flour.\n A single fine, dry particle of earth or other material; grain of dust.","Fine, dry particles of matter found in the air and covering the surface of objects, typically consisting of soil lifted up by the wind, pollen, hair, fiber debris, dead skin cells, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To remove dust from.","To remove dust; to clean by removing dust."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dust"}],"entries":[{"title":"Durango","blocks":[{"text":"Durango, officially the Free and Sovereign State of Durango, is one of the states which make up the 32 federal entities of Mexico, situated in the northwest portion of the country. With a population of 1,832,650, the eighth lowest of Mexico's states, Durango has Mexico's second-lowest population density, after Baja California Sur. The capital city, Victoria de Durango, is named after the first President of Mexico, Guadalupe Victoria."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/R%C3%ADo%2C_Monta%C3%B1a%2C_Durango_%2816697897432%29.jpg/330px-R%C3%ADo%2C_Monta%C3%B1a%2C_Durango_%2816697897432%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Durango","wikidata":"Q79918"},{"title":"Dust","blocks":[{"text":"Dust is made of fine particles of solid matter. On Earth, it generally consists of particles in the atmosphere that come from various sources such as soil lifted by wind, volcanic eruptions, and pollution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Dust_storm_approaching_Stratford%2C_Texas.jpg/330px-Dust_storm_approaching_Stratford%2C_Texas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dust","wikidata":"Q165632"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Barrancas_en_parque_natural_mexiquillo.jpg/500px-Barrancas_en_parque_natural_mexiquillo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Barrancas_en_parque_natural_mexiquillo.jpg/1280px-Barrancas_en_parque_natural_mexiquillo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Barrancas_en_parque_natural_mexiquillo.jpg/500px-Barrancas_en_parque_natural_mexiquillo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View toward the canyon at the Mexiquillo nature reserve","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarrancas_en_parque_natural_mexiquillo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Tortuga_del_bols%C3%B3n.jpg/500px-Tortuga_del_bols%C3%B3n.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Tortuga_del_bols%C3%B3n.jpg/1280px-Tortuga_del_bols%C3%B3n.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Tortuga_del_bols%C3%B3n.jpg/500px-Tortuga_del_bols%C3%B3n.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Desert tortoise in the Mapimí Biosphere Reserve","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATortuga_del_bols%C3%B3n.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c